     "title": "Grasping the relationship of requirements and constraints to the solution",
     "body": "<p><em>According to the curriculum, chapter 6 as a whole is not exam-relevant.</em></p><p>Using at least one concrete example system, understand <strong>why</strong> the architecture looks the way it does: which requirements – especially quality goals – and which constraints (technical, organizational, legal) led to which solution decisions? This makes the relationship <strong>requirement → decision → structure</strong> from chapters 2 to 4 tangible.</p>"
