     "body": "<p><em>According to the curriculum, chapter 6 as a whole is not exam-relevant.</em></p><p>Using at least one example, understand the <strong>technical implementation</strong> of a solution: implementation, technical concepts, products used and solution strategies. The aim is to understand what building blocks, cross-cutting concepts and deployment look like in a real system.</p><details class='refdeep'><summary>🧭 Deep dive & examples <span class='rl'>not exam-relevant</span></summary><p class='refdeepnote'>For understanding and taken from the training slides – goes beyond the curriculum’s learning goals and does not need to be learned separately.</p><div class='refbox extra'><b>➕ Extra knowledge – not exam-relevant, can be skipped</b><p>Good sources are publicly documented example architectures, such as the examples on the arc42 website.</p></div></details>"
